the last time I was in India it had all  become a familiar scene the rickshaws  rumbling through busy bazaars shoppers  haggling over everything from gemstones  to silk saris pilgrims prostrating their  way to salvation and street food  enhanced by locally sourced infectious  pathogens this time around I knew the  country had changed I wanted to see the  effects of 13 years of market reform and  hyper growth since my last visit  so I summoned an uber already something  new and I headed 15 miles south of my  Delhi hotel  [Music]  and as the crumbling roads of the  capital city opened up into a thirty-two  lane Expressway the old India that I  thought I knew began to look like a  thing of the past I had arrived in the  city of Gurgaon  [Music]  it's hard to imagine but 25 years ago  there was nothing here no high-rises no  kitchen shopping malls with Vegas live  Trump low ceilings no 27 hole Jack  Nicklaus Signature golf courses  [Music]  stretching all the way back to medieval  times Gurgaon was nothing more than a  plot of rocky soil with a small market  place and no railway link to the rest of  the country but Gurgaon had one enormous  advantage over other Indian cities it  had no municipal government most people  did not even know Gurgaon existed thirty  years ago it was a completely a farmland  on the outskirts of Delhi Gurgaon was a  sleepy dusty quiet town with lots of  agricultural land that was barren it is  KP Singh who started this company called  DLF and that company has pretty much  single-handedly build the city when  Delhi banned private real estate  development in the 1950s crucial pal  singh began buying land south of the  city limits his company Delhi land and  Finance offered cash and equity stakes  to farmers in Gurgaon many of these cow  herds became instant crore patties  millionaires in local lingo while KP  Singh would become the fifth richest man  in India by the turn of the century  acquiring land is a biggest problem  across the world and the government's  use their eminent domain powers to  acquire any large tract of land for any  development but here your case where  whole city has been built almost all by  acquiring land voluntary transaction the  province made it easier here to change  agricultural land into commercial or  residential or industrial land and set  up factories  [Music]  maruti was the first to arrive with an  auto manufacturing plant in the 1980s as  india step back from socialism in the  1990s foreign investment bypassed Delhi  and poured straight into Gurgaon when  General Electric set up shop hundreds of  multinationals followed suit soon  Gurgaon was generating middle-class jobs  by the hundreds of thousands today it  boasts an absurd 30 percent annual  growth rate and the third highest per  capita income in India under the shops  and establishments Act at that time  women could not work beyond 6 p.m. now  once that law got changed in Haryana and  very early it allowed a lot of young  women to start working in the service  sector in Google to work largely through  the night because we were matching over  times with times across the Atlantic and  the Pacific the first private developer  was DLF and DLF therefore took it upon  itself to build roads in go down to  later see wage lines to monitor law in  order  DLF in in a lot of ways set up its own  security even now you will find that  most of us here in Google hire our own  security and that is what keeps it  largely crime free while Gurgaon isn't  actually crime free it doesn't lack for  protection either 35,000 private  security guards keep a watchful eye on  the city compared with only 3,000 public  officers so why do businesses flock to  Gurgaon when taxpayers will pick up the  bills elsewhere it's high cost to come  here hire your own security bill your  own power plants extract groundwater  have your own transportation Google  didn't have local transportation till a  decade ago so it is expensive but look  at the other side of the picture it's  high quality because there is high  competition there are a lot of private  players you have very high quality  service Gurgaon services and cleanliness  are like nothing else I've seen in the  country  India's only privately run metro system  is fast modern and efficient employees  compulsively sweep floors that already  look spotless  it's unclear if Gorgons Metro turns a  profit but as it increases the value of  land owned by DLF and others it may have  already accomplished its mission over  time other developers have entered the  market competing with DLF and diluting  its share of Gurgaon real estate but as  DLF remains the dominant provider of  roads utilities security even India's  only private fire department it raises  the question of whether India's largest  commercial real estate company is  actually a private government we have  not allowed them to become private  government they have been sort of a  government within specific areas that  they have developed the common property  the public land which they have to leave  open for public infrastructure obviously  it's not under their control in google  it appears a little incongruous because  you have these neighborhoods which are  very high quality and then you  immediately step out and you see it all  disappear inside a compound of a colony  you will find great services well class  standards right outside that gate public  services don't exist so water  connections are very poor sewage lines  are not done very well it's in a sense  story of India frankly where the private  initiative has been very successful has  created world-class standards and  aspirations among the people right while  the public sector has not been able to  keep up with that the state was willing  to do just enough to collect the high  levels of revenue that a flourishing  town like Google could provide them with  but was unwilling to invest any of that  back into the city's infrastructure one  simple way to assess success is do  people want to go there our people are  going to go there willingly willing to  settle there open their businesses  invest large amounts of money in  developing those areas I think on all of  those counts google has been fabulously  successful while cities  blossom and bloom like this the flipside  is that they will have a tendency to  become extremely polluted and a tendency  to to to have large amounts of  population living in slums slums are  places where there is no public utility  we have no education no sanitation in  swans  [Music]  16% of Gorgons population lives in slums  like this one if that seems like a lot  to you the shocker is that it's less  than the average Indian city there are a  hundred and fifty million fewer poor  people in India since my last visit 13  years ago that's half the population of  the United States lifted out of the  slums India's achievements over the past  decade are inspiring but as my own  country turns its back on the same  global markets that transformed a rocky  patch of farmland into a metropolis of 2  million souls I can only hope that  Gurgaon has many years of hyper growth  yet to come  Oh  [Music]  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

